From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dawid Wesierski <dawid.wesierski@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net/iavf: fix init of VF left active by killed process

When a process that uses an iavf VF ends without iavf_dev_close(), for
example when it is killed, the VF does not send VIRTCHNL_OP_RESET_VF.
The PF keeps the resources that the process negotiated, and the VF
stays active.

On Linux, vfio-pci resets the function when the next process opens the
device, and the PF then resets its VF state. A bus driver that does no
reset, such as NetUIO on Windows, keeps the VF active. The out-of-tree
ice PF driver rejects OP_GET_VF_RESOURCES for an active VF, and the
next probe fails:

  iavf_wait_for_msg(): Return failure -5 for cmd 3
  iavf_get_vf_resource(): Failed to execute command of OP_GET_VF_RESOURCE
  iavf_init_vf(): iavf_get_vf_config failed
  iavf_dev_init(): Init vf failed

The host logs "PF failed to honor VF 0, opcode 3, error -22". Each new
probe fails the same way. Only a reset of the VF clears the state.

When OP_GET_VF_RESOURCES fails at probe, request a VF reset, wait for
the PF to start and complete it, initialize the admin queue again, and
do the version and resource steps once more. This is the reset sequence
of iavf_dev_close() and iavf_init_vf() on a port reset. A successful
init does not change. The reset recovery, which has just reset the VF,
does not retry.

Fixes: 22b123a36d07 ("net/avf: initialize PMD")
Cc: stable@dpdk.org

Signed-off-by: Dawid Wesierski <dawid.wesierski@intel.com>
---
 drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_ethdev.c | 36 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_ethdev.c b/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_ethdev.c
index d800a3382a..2ead88447c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_ethdev.c
+++ b/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_ethdev.c
@@ -2627,6 +2627,36 @@ iavf_init_proto_xtr(struct rte_eth_dev *dev)
 	}
 }
 
+static int
+iavf_reset_and_renegotiate(struct iavf_adapter *adapter)
+{
+	struct iavf_hw *hw = IAVF_DEV_PRIVATE_TO_HW(adapter);
+
+	PMD_INIT_LOG(WARNING, "Reset VF and retry init");
+
+	if (iavf_vf_reset(hw) != IAVF_SUCCESS || !iavf_is_reset_detected(adapter)) {
+		PMD_INIT_LOG(ERR, "VF reset not started");
+		return -1;
+	}
+	iavf_shutdown_adminq(hw);
+
+	if (iavf_check_vf_reset_done(hw) != 0) {
+		PMD_INIT_LOG(ERR, "VF is still resetting");
+		return -1;
+	}
+
+	iavf_init_adminq_parameter(hw);
+	if (iavf_init_adminq(hw) != IAVF_SUCCESS) {
+		PMD_INIT_LOG(ERR, "init_adminq failed");
+		return -1;
+	}
+
+	if (iavf_check_api_version(adapter) != 0)
+		return -1;
+
+	return iavf_get_vf_resource(adapter);
+}
+
 static int
 iavf_init_vf(struct rte_eth_dev *dev)
 {
@@ -2676,7 +2706,11 @@ iavf_init_vf(struct rte_eth_dev *dev)
 		goto err_api;
 	}
 
-	if (iavf_get_vf_resource(adapter) != 0) {
+	err = iavf_get_vf_resource(adapter);
+	/* A probe can find the VF still active from a killed process: reset it once. */
+	if (err != 0 && !vf->in_reset_recovery)
+		err = iavf_reset_and_renegotiate(adapter);
+	if (err != 0) {
 		PMD_INIT_LOG(ERR, "iavf_get_vf_config failed");
 		goto err_alloc;
 	}
-- 
